= extend('layout')

.hero.main.centered
  .container
    h2 Manage Multiple Projects with Ease
    h4.subtitle Consistent development environments, and lightning fast static site hosting using Nitrous PubStorm.

    a.btn.btn-lg.btn-default href="#"
      | Get Started for Free

.hero.featurette
  .container
    h2 All your client projects, in one place
    h4.subtitle
      | Create isolated, shareable development environments for each of your projects.
    img.feature.full.img-responsive src="/images/dashboard-next-agencies.png"

.hero.featurette.dual.peakaboo
  .container
    .row
      .col-xs-12.col-md-5
        h2 Snapshot
        h4.subtitle
          | Preserve the state of your project's environment, and revert back to them at any time
      .col-xs-12.col-md-7
        .full-visual
          img.feature src="/images/snapshots-next-agencies.png" width="970px"

.hero.featurette.dual.peakaboo
  .container
    .row
      .col-xs-12.col-md-5
        h2 Manage Team Members
        h4.subtitle
          | Quickly add and remove team members, set project access and more.

      .col-xs-12.col-md-7
        img.feature src="/images/members-next-agencies.png" width="970px"

article.blockquote.rails
  .container
    .row
      .col-xs-12.col-md-8.col-md-offset-2
        blockquote
          img.blockquote-image src="/images/customers/klabnik.png" alt="klabnik logo"
          . I know how to administer a computer well enough,
          span.highlight but I don't want to.
          |  Nitrous allows me to say "I want to code some Rails now, kthx" and not have to worry about getting the details right every time. Sometimes, I care about the details, but most of the time, I don't.

          .author
            | Steve Klabnik,
            span.bio Rails Core Committer & prolific Open Source contributor

article.blockquote.wilsonsmith
  .container
    .row
      .col-xs-12.col-md-8.col-md-offset-2
        blockquote
          img.blockquote-image src="/images/customers/wilsonsmith.svg" alt="wilsonsmith logo"
          . I love the vision. It has been prophesied by the forefathers of UNIX that a day would come in which our computers would simply be a piece of glass connected to some computer on the network.
          span.highlight Nitrous is making that dream a reality.
          .  Practically speaking, the feature that captivates my attention is that I have
          span.highlight easy SSH access to a Linux machine that someone else is maintaining.
          |  Among all of my responsibilities, personal system administration is something that I am keen on delegating. If I never have to worry about keeping a machine online and its state secured, then I will be winning.

          .author
            | Ryan Smith
            span.bio Partner, Wilson &amp; Smith Consulting

= partial('partials/cta')